00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:50.150 line:0%
- Joining me today
is an army veteran,

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:53.486 line:0%
a former democratic US
presidential candidate

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:56.423 align:start size:97% position:3%
and now former
Congresswoman, Tulsi Gabbard.

00:00:56.423 --> 00:00:58.458 align:start size:84% position:16%
Welcome back to
the "Rubin Report."

00:00:58.458 --> 00:01:00.760
- Hey, good to see
you, Dave, always.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:03.530
- So there's obviously
a ton to talk about here

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:06.633
and a lot of stuff happening
right now as we tape this,

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:08.902
but first off do I
have to refer to you

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:10.737
as former Congresswoman?

00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:13.406
Do you keep being called
Congresswoman forever?

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:14.874
How does that work?

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:16.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like when when you're
mayor they always call you

00:01:16.309 --> 00:01:19.212
Mr. Mayor or Mr. President,

00:01:19.212 --> 00:01:21.281 align:start size:84% position:16%
are you Congresswoman
Tulsi forever,

00:01:21.281 --> 00:01:22.782
even though you've stepped away?

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:25.618 line:0%
- I think so, but I don't
know the answer to that.

00:01:25.618 --> 00:01:28.688 line:0%
My former staff asked
me that yesterday,

00:01:28.688 --> 00:01:29.889 line:0%
I was like, you know what?

00:01:29.889 --> 00:01:31.224
I actually don't know
the answer to that

00:01:31.224 --> 00:01:34.260
but Tulsi is always great.

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:35.595
- Tulsi will work.

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:39.165
Okay, so look, we're
taping this right now

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:43.069 align:start size:88% position:13%
as the Capitol is
literally being stormed.

00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:44.637 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, that is
happening right now.

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:46.372
I know you were seeing it
right before we started

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:47.507
just as I was.

00:01:49.075 --> 00:01:50.610
I wasn't planning
on starting here

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:53.780 align:start size:94% position:6%
but what do you make of
what's going on right now?

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:57.617 align:start size:97% position:3%
- I mean, it's heartbreaking
to see this happening

00:01:57.617 --> 00:02:02.522
at our nation's capital,
but it is also indicative.

00:02:03.957 --> 00:02:07.360 align:start size:97% position:3%
This is a symptom of much
deeper issues and challenges

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:09.996 align:start size:84% position:16%
that have been stewing
for a long time.

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:14.167
And a lot, especially as of
late, over this last year

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:18.204
where this conflict culture
that we have seen growing

00:02:18.204 --> 00:02:22.542 align:start size:97% position:3%
in our society, whether it's
online and now it's being

00:02:24.077 --> 00:02:27.780
embodied or actioned offline,

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:30.450 align:start size:84% position:16%
it results in
something like this.

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:33.319
And so you've got to look at

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:35.588
what's driving this,
what's fueling it.

00:02:35.588 --> 00:02:38.925 align:start size:97% position:3%
You can look at politicians,
political leaders,

00:02:38.925 --> 00:02:42.428 align:start size:84% position:16%
who are more
interested in fueling

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:47.433 align:start size:97% position:3%
and yeah fueling
divisiveness, riling people up

00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:51.638
for their own personal
or political benefit.

00:02:51.638 --> 00:02:55.875 align:start size:97% position:3%
You see the media doing
the same thing for ratings.

00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:58.111
You see these big
tech monopolies

00:02:58.111 --> 00:03:01.214 align:start size:97% position:3%
in Facebook using
algorithms and social media

00:03:01.214 --> 00:03:05.585
to continue to push and push
and put fuel on the flames

00:03:05.585 --> 00:03:07.287
of this divisiveness.

00:03:07.287 --> 00:03:10.323
Well, you see what is
happening here today

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:13.059 align:start size:97% position:3%
at the United States
Capitol before our very eyes

00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:14.661
is the manifestation of that.

00:03:14.661 --> 00:03:17.630
That is the symptom of
these deeper problems.

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:19.499 align:start size:84% position:16%
And from a leadership
perspective,

00:03:19.499 --> 00:03:23.369
I think this is where
you've got to look

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:26.839
to the kind of leadership
we need but don't have

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:28.341
in this country right now.

00:03:28.341 --> 00:03:30.243
Which is leadership that puts
the wellbeing of the people

00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:33.880 align:start size:97% position:3%
and country before themselves,
before political power,

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:36.950
before their selfish ambition.

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:38.751
- Are you kind of
shocked as someone

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:42.989
that was in the government that
just not only our leadership

00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:45.225 align:start size:88% position:13%
in terms of government,
but our leadership

00:03:45.225 --> 00:03:47.827
sort of across the board,
our academic leadership,

00:03:47.827 --> 00:03:50.563 align:start size:97% position:3%
our intellectual leadership,
there's podcasters

00:03:50.563 --> 00:03:54.334
and stuff like that, but that
we don't have sort of like

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:57.804
a trusted group
of people anymore

00:03:57.804 --> 00:04:00.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
that kind of bring us
together across the board?

00:04:00.006 --> 00:04:02.275
It almost just simply
doesn't exist anymore.

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:05.178
- I think that's right.

00:04:05.178 --> 00:04:09.115 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I think that it's become
such a segmented thing

00:04:09.115 --> 00:04:12.785 align:start size:97% position:3%
where you have whether it's
a political leadership,

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:15.255
those in the media or those a
new media or whatever it is,

00:04:15.255 --> 00:04:18.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
you have these these
quote unquote influencers

00:04:18.291 --> 00:04:22.562
that are only speaking to
their segment of people

00:04:22.562 --> 00:04:24.897
who agree with them or
believe the same things

00:04:24.897 --> 00:04:26.099
that they believe.

00:04:26.099 --> 00:04:30.203 align:start size:88% position:13%
And there's no exposure,
real civil discourse

00:04:30.203 --> 00:04:32.305
or dialogue to people who
might have different views,

00:04:32.305 --> 00:04:33.773
different opinions,
different beliefs,

00:04:33.773 --> 00:04:36.576
different political positions.

00:04:36.576 --> 00:04:40.113
And I think it's not
only not a good thing

00:04:40.113 --> 00:04:44.917
for our country, but I
think also contributes

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:47.520 align:start size:97% position:3%
especially when you're
using this divisive rhetoric

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:51.391
and language that can help fuel

00:04:51.391 --> 00:04:53.192
those who then get
riled up and say,

00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:54.694
oh, actually, you know what?

00:04:54.694 --> 00:04:56.829
I'm gonna go take action on
this because those people,

00:04:56.829 --> 00:04:58.831
they are my enemy.

00:04:58.831 --> 00:05:00.133
That's the dangerous thing.

00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:01.634
- So does this what's
happening right now

00:05:01.634 --> 00:05:02.835
and then we'll move on
to some other stuff.

00:05:02.835 --> 00:05:05.271 align:start size:88% position:13%
Does it sort of feel
like this was inevitable

00:05:05.271 --> 00:05:06.472
in a weird way?

00:05:06.472 --> 00:05:08.675 align:start size:88% position:13%
Like once I started
seeing it this morning,

00:05:08.675 --> 00:05:11.044
it was just kinda like, oh yeah,

00:05:11.044 --> 00:05:13.913
of course this is exactly
what was gonna happen.

00:05:13.913 --> 00:05:17.617 align:start size:97% position:3%
And in a weird way, it's
almost like we all deserve it

00:05:17.617 --> 00:05:20.620
for being part of it
or something like that.

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:25.625
- Well, I was, oh
gosh, months ago,

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:29.896
months ago was maybe one
of a few people who warned

00:05:29.896 --> 00:05:34.901
of a civil war if we continue
down the path that we are on.

00:05:36.703 --> 00:05:39.539 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I think that what
we are seeing now

00:05:39.539 --> 00:05:44.110 align:start size:97% position:3%
with this divisiveness that
exists very much online

00:05:45.511 --> 00:05:48.081 align:start size:94% position:6%
now being translated into
action further points

00:05:48.081 --> 00:05:49.315
in that direction.

00:05:49.315 --> 00:05:52.518
Unless we, as a country
do something about it.

00:05:52.518 --> 00:05:54.220
We as the American people,

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:56.389
we as leaders in this country,

00:05:56.389 --> 00:06:00.059 align:start size:84% position:16%
unless we shift course
and start leading

00:06:01.794 --> 00:06:03.529
for the interest of the public,

00:06:03.529 --> 00:06:05.631
the American people,
servant leadership,

00:06:05.631 --> 00:06:07.367
leaders who are in
positions of power

00:06:07.367 --> 00:06:09.235
whether they're elected
or not elected saying,

00:06:09.235 --> 00:06:12.438 align:start position:0%
I am here to serve this
country and the American people

00:06:12.438 --> 00:06:16.409
not my party, not my
political interests,

00:06:16.409 --> 00:06:19.479 align:start size:94% position:6%
not my political ambition
or selfish, money.

00:06:19.479 --> 00:06:22.382 align:start size:84% position:16%
Whatever that selfish
driver may be,

00:06:22.382 --> 00:06:24.484 align:start size:88% position:13%
we need servant leaders
in place leading

00:06:24.484 --> 00:06:26.419 align:start size:81% position:19%
with what we in
Hawaii call Aloha.

00:06:26.419 --> 00:06:27.954
You and I have talked
about this before.

00:06:27.954 --> 00:06:30.790
Aloha is saying,
hey, I respect you.

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:35.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
I open my heart and I love
you as a fellow person

00:06:35.428 --> 00:06:39.966
as a child of God,
as a fellow American.

00:06:39.966 --> 00:06:42.301 align:start size:97% position:3%
And whether we agree or
disagree on different issues,

00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:45.538 align:start size:97% position:3%
whether we come from
different backgrounds or not,

00:06:45.538 --> 00:06:47.507
we've gotta be able to
come together on this

00:06:47.507 --> 00:06:49.942
shared common ground and
work for the betterment

00:06:49.942 --> 00:06:52.745
and the wellbeing
of the country.

00:06:52.745 --> 00:06:55.515 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I think just one last--
- [Dave] So what do you think,

00:06:55.515 --> 00:06:58.317 align:start size:94% position:6%
- I was just gonna say one
last note on the danger

00:06:58.317 --> 00:07:00.920 align:start size:84% position:16%
of what we are seeing
playing out today

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:05.892
is this normalization of
violence where violence

00:07:06.993 --> 00:07:09.328 align:start size:84% position:16%
and a lot of the
riots that we've seen

00:07:09.328 --> 00:07:10.730 align:start size:81% position:19%
over the last year
are occurring.

00:07:10.730 --> 00:07:13.266
That violence is somehow okay

00:07:13.266 --> 00:07:18.271
if it aligns with your view
of what these people are,

00:07:19.138 --> 00:07:21.340
quote unquote fighting for.

00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:23.409
And that's, that's a
very dangerous thing

00:07:23.409 --> 00:07:25.578
because when I say
leading with Aloha,

00:07:25.578 --> 00:07:27.113
I don't mean just,

00:07:27.113 --> 00:07:29.182
okay we're just gonna sit
back and not do anything.

00:07:29.182 --> 00:07:31.217
Leading with Aloha means
standing up and fighting

00:07:31.217 --> 00:07:34.921 align:start size:97% position:3%
for what is right but doing
so within the construct

00:07:34.921 --> 00:07:38.090
of the institutions that
we have in this country.

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:41.194
For example, if
you are concerned

00:07:41.194 --> 00:07:46.199
about the legitimacy and the
integrity of our elections,

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:49.368
take action to do something.

00:07:49.368 --> 00:07:51.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
I introduced a bill called
The Securing America's

00:07:51.337 --> 00:07:54.874
Election Act that if
our country's leaders

00:07:54.874 --> 00:07:57.243
had passed would have prevented

00:07:57.243 --> 00:07:59.779
a lot of the the angst
that people are feeling

00:07:59.779 --> 00:08:01.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
and seeing right now
with this election saying

00:08:01.414 --> 00:08:04.083
that you have to
have a paper trail.

00:08:04.083 --> 00:08:06.252 align:start size:84% position:16%
You have to have an
auditable paper backup

00:08:06.252 --> 00:08:07.820
for any electronic system.

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:09.989 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
So that there's no doubt
or question in mind

00:08:09.989 --> 00:08:12.492 line:0%
if there has been a hack attempt

00:08:12.492 --> 00:08:16.295 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
or some attempt to manipulate
our votes as voters.

00:08:16.295 --> 00:08:17.964 align:start size:84% position:16%
If all of these
people in Congress,

00:08:17.964 --> 00:08:21.567
Democrat and Republican had
taken that issue seriously

00:08:21.567 --> 00:08:24.270 align:start size:97% position:3%
and passed that legislation,
those who are now saying,

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:25.771 align:start size:84% position:16%
hey, we have to
stand up for the...

00:08:25.771 --> 00:08:28.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
Why don't you do
something about it before?

00:08:28.708 --> 00:08:31.477
We do need to stand up and
fight for the well-being

00:08:31.477 --> 00:08:33.946
of this country, stand
up for our constitution,

00:08:33.946 --> 00:08:36.282 align:start size:84% position:16%
uphold it but we need
to do it in a way

00:08:36.282 --> 00:08:40.786
that is constructive and
within the institutions

00:08:40.786 --> 00:08:44.090 align:start size:97% position:3%
that have been set up in this
society, that is America.

00:08:44.090 --> 00:08:47.293 align:start size:97% position:3%
- So I have no doubt that
probably every single person

00:08:47.293 --> 00:08:49.195
watching this right now
is agreeing with you

00:08:49.195 --> 00:08:51.264 align:start size:84% position:16%
and going, okay,
that all makes sense.

00:08:51.264 --> 00:08:52.198
I'm on board.

00:08:52.198 --> 00:08:54.066
So Tulsi why'd you get out?

00:08:55.268 --> 00:08:57.036
Like you're exactly
what we need, right?

00:08:57.036 --> 00:08:59.405 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, I mean, I've tweeted
it a million times.

00:08:59.405 --> 00:09:02.708 align:start position:0%
If Tulsi Gabbard was the
future of the democratic party,

00:09:02.708 --> 00:09:05.311 align:start size:94% position:6%
I could honestly consider
myself a Democrat.

00:09:05.311 --> 00:09:06.512
I can't do that anymore.

00:09:06.512 --> 00:09:08.514
I don't consider
myself a Republican

00:09:08.514 --> 00:09:11.050 align:start size:94% position:6%
but what you just said
there, I think most people

00:09:11.050 --> 00:09:13.886
agree with, yet at the same
time you are getting out.

00:09:13.886 --> 00:09:15.855
So tell me about that.

00:09:15.855 --> 00:09:17.557
- I had to make
a decision, Dave.

00:09:17.557 --> 00:09:18.891
And I had to make a decision,

00:09:18.891 --> 00:09:22.161 align:start size:84% position:16%
I made this decision
last fall of 2019

00:09:22.161 --> 00:09:24.063 align:start size:84% position:16%
as I was campaigning
for president.

00:09:24.063 --> 00:09:27.166
It was a frankly, a
practical decision

00:09:27.166 --> 00:09:30.202
where I could not both run
for reelection to Congress

00:09:30.202 --> 00:09:33.039
and continue running for
president at the same time.

00:09:33.039 --> 00:09:37.343
And I made the decision
to run for president.

00:09:37.343 --> 00:09:38.878
It was a very serious decision

00:09:38.878 --> 00:09:40.379
that was well thought through.

00:09:40.379 --> 00:09:43.683
And I made the decision
to continue that campaign

00:09:43.683 --> 00:09:47.954 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the presidency because
of the grave issues

00:09:47.954 --> 00:09:50.256
that I was raising
in that campaign

00:09:50.256 --> 00:09:52.491 align:start position:0%
and the kind of change in
leadership that I really believe

00:09:52.491 --> 00:09:54.026
our country needs.

00:09:54.026 --> 00:09:57.229
So I'm gonna continue to fight.

00:09:57.229 --> 00:10:00.266 align:start size:97% position:3%
I may not be in Congress
anymore as of a few days ago

00:10:00.266 --> 00:10:02.368
but I'm gonna continue
to advocate for freedom.

00:10:02.368 --> 00:10:06.072 align:start size:97% position:3%
I'm gonna continue to advocate
for common sense solutions

00:10:06.072 --> 00:10:08.207
in our society and
in our government.

00:10:08.207 --> 00:10:12.244
And to continue to bring the
truth to the conversations

00:10:12.244 --> 00:10:14.313 align:start size:84% position:16%
that we as a country
should be having.

00:10:14.313 --> 00:10:16.015
- So speaking of the truth,

00:10:17.183 --> 00:10:18.417
I mean, I'm just putting
my cards on the table.

00:10:18.417 --> 00:10:20.920
I find you to be
one of the last,

00:10:20.920 --> 00:10:22.388
I guess you're not
a politician anymore

00:10:22.388 --> 00:10:26.425
but one of the last, somewhat
honest politicians, right?

00:10:26.425 --> 00:10:28.060
I sense that you're
really trying to do

00:10:28.060 --> 00:10:29.261
something decent here.

00:10:29.261 --> 00:10:31.998 align:start size:84% position:16%
Can you just talk
about what it was like

00:10:31.998 --> 00:10:34.333
to go through the
democratic machine

00:10:34.333 --> 00:10:38.304
during the primary process and
go through the media machine

00:10:38.304 --> 00:10:40.606
during that, the way
the media treated you

00:10:40.606 --> 00:10:44.443 align:start size:97% position:3%
and that insane comment
that Hillary made about you,

00:10:44.443 --> 00:10:47.113 align:start size:97% position:3%
and that little tussle that
you got in with Kamala,

00:10:47.113 --> 00:10:48.614
all of those things.

00:10:48.614 --> 00:10:51.584 align:start size:97% position:3%
While it was like, I was
seeing so many people online

00:10:51.584 --> 00:10:54.286
that were like, I can't
be a Democrat anymore

00:10:54.286 --> 00:10:57.289
but I kinda like her,
that's the direction.

00:10:57.289 --> 00:11:01.527
And yet the party, the way the
party in effect treated you.

00:11:01.527 --> 00:11:05.031 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Yeah, we could do a
whole show just on this.

00:11:05.031 --> 00:11:07.199
But I'll point to--
- Come on get on your

00:11:07.199 --> 00:11:08.534
(indistinct), let's go.

00:11:08.534 --> 00:11:10.603
- A couple of the
major takeaways

00:11:10.603 --> 00:11:13.105 align:start size:84% position:16%
that I had from
that experience is,

00:11:14.540 --> 00:11:19.545 align:start size:97% position:3%
the danger and the threat
that is posed to our democracy

00:11:20.880 --> 00:11:24.116 align:start size:97% position:3%
by the power of our political
parties, both of them.

00:11:24.116 --> 00:11:27.720 align:start size:81% position:19%
And the power that
the media has.

00:11:27.720 --> 00:11:32.692
A lot of people talk about
needing to reform our money

00:11:32.692 --> 00:11:35.995
in politics and make sure
that it's more transparent.

00:11:35.995 --> 00:11:37.430
And I agree with a lot
of all those things,

00:11:37.430 --> 00:11:39.999
they are necessary
but nobody points to

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:44.003
the effect that the media has

00:11:44.003 --> 00:11:47.773 align:start size:97% position:3%
and the billions of
dollars that that exposure,

00:11:47.773 --> 00:11:50.576 align:start size:88% position:13%
that narrative that
they're pushing is worth

00:11:50.576 --> 00:11:54.480
and how they are filtering
what kind of information

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:56.782
voters are getting access to.

00:11:56.782 --> 00:11:58.951
I'll throw big tech
in with this as well,

00:11:58.951 --> 00:12:00.453
because they're the
Google, Facebook,

00:12:00.453 --> 00:12:03.089
they're doing the exact
same thing and deciding,

00:12:03.089 --> 00:12:04.090
hey this is,

00:12:04.090 --> 00:12:05.624
this or these are the candidates

00:12:05.624 --> 00:12:07.126
who we want you to hear from.

00:12:07.126 --> 00:12:11.330
Here's the narrative that
we want you to hear or see.

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:15.201
And in my case, they
chose their narrative.

00:12:15.201 --> 00:12:18.037
They chose their candidates
and ultimately they decided

00:12:18.037 --> 00:12:20.172
that they didn't want
voters to hear from me.

00:12:20.172 --> 00:12:21.774
- But who is they?

00:12:21.774 --> 00:12:23.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause I feel like it
always comes down to this.

00:12:23.309 --> 00:12:24.276 align:start size:84% position:16%
Like certain people
will be like,

00:12:24.276 --> 00:12:26.045
okay, it's the Clinton machine

00:12:26.045 --> 00:12:27.613
that runs the democratic party

00:12:27.613 --> 00:12:29.648 align:start size:81% position:19%
or maybe that's
kind of crumbling,

00:12:29.648 --> 00:12:31.283
now it's more the Obama machine.

00:12:31.283 --> 00:12:32.518
Like when you say that,

00:12:32.518 --> 00:12:34.787 align:start size:84% position:16%
like that the party
didn't want you there,

00:12:34.787 --> 00:12:37.556 align:start size:84% position:16%
in effect or big tech,
all those pieces,

00:12:37.556 --> 00:12:40.326
like who is they, do you think?

00:12:40.326 --> 00:12:41.527
People ask me this all the time.

00:12:41.527 --> 00:12:43.496 align:start size:88% position:13%
I don't know that anyone
has a good answer.

00:12:43.496 --> 00:12:46.499 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Ultimately it is
whether it's the people

00:12:46.499 --> 00:12:49.001 align:start size:88% position:13%
who hold these positions
of power, literally.

00:12:50.202 --> 00:12:52.772
The heads of these
media institutions,

00:12:52.772 --> 00:12:55.341
these for-profit corporations

00:12:55.341 --> 00:12:59.445
who are supposedly
generating news.

00:12:59.445 --> 00:13:02.214
But also it's both the people

00:13:02.214 --> 00:13:03.682 align:start size:84% position:16%
who are in charge
of political parties

00:13:03.682 --> 00:13:06.652 align:start position:0%
but also the people who are
maybe more institutional people.

00:13:06.652 --> 00:13:08.554
Like the Clintons, for example.

00:13:10.990 --> 00:13:13.893 align:start position:0%
I came and spoke the truth
about a lot of different issues

00:13:13.893 --> 00:13:17.863 align:start size:88% position:13%
from our foreign policy
and how destructive

00:13:17.863 --> 00:13:22.134 align:start size:88% position:13%
this foreign policy
has been largely led by

00:13:22.134 --> 00:13:24.136
people like Hillary
Clinton and others,

00:13:24.136 --> 00:13:27.606
and the cost that it has
carried both to soldiers

00:13:27.606 --> 00:13:31.110
and friends and veterans who I
know and who I've served with

00:13:31.110 --> 00:13:33.779
but also to every
single American.

00:13:33.779 --> 00:13:36.482
Bringing the truth and
calling out big tech,

00:13:36.482 --> 00:13:37.950
calling out the media.

00:13:37.950 --> 00:13:42.521 align:start position:0%
This is something that they
felt they didn't want to happen.

00:13:43.255 --> 00:13:47.226
And so those two areas

00:13:48.127 --> 00:13:51.931
really take away the opportunity

00:13:51.931 --> 00:13:53.365 align:start size:84% position:16%
whether you're talking
about the power

00:13:53.365 --> 00:13:55.100
the political parties
have through the money

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:56.368
that they're able to raise,

00:13:56.368 --> 00:13:57.970 align:start size:84% position:16%
unlimited amounts
of money essentially

00:13:57.970 --> 00:14:02.474
and leverage those dollars
to pressure individuals,

00:14:02.474 --> 00:14:05.177 align:start size:88% position:13%
members of Congress,
state political parties,

00:14:05.177 --> 00:14:06.979
to do what they want,

00:14:06.979 --> 00:14:08.848
as well as the power
that the media has.

00:14:08.848 --> 00:14:10.749
These are the things that
are getting in the way

00:14:10.749 --> 00:14:13.319 align:start size:97% position:3%
of the American people
being able to get the truth

00:14:13.319 --> 00:14:16.255
and to be shown, hey,
here are the choices

00:14:16.255 --> 00:14:18.724
that you have to vote
for in this election.

00:14:18.724 --> 00:14:21.093
Let's have a fair hearing
of what they stand for,

00:14:21.093 --> 00:14:22.494 align:start size:84% position:16%
what kind of
leadership they bring,

00:14:22.494 --> 00:14:24.496 align:start size:97% position:3%
the qualifications,
experience that they bring,

00:14:24.496 --> 00:14:27.199 align:start size:84% position:16%
what kind of judgment
they'll exercise.

00:14:27.199 --> 00:14:30.569
Frankly, that's not happening.

00:14:30.569 --> 00:14:32.304 align:start size:84% position:16%
That's not happening
in our election.

00:14:32.304 --> 00:14:33.839
- So speaking of
the big tech thing,

00:14:33.839 --> 00:14:36.408
are you still involved in
that lawsuit with YouTube?

00:14:37.776 --> 00:14:39.144
- With Google, no.

00:14:40.546 --> 00:14:43.782
We ended up having
to drop the lawsuit.

00:14:43.782 --> 00:14:45.784
Or actually, no, I
think with that one,

00:14:45.784 --> 00:14:47.019
I've been involved
in a couple here.

00:14:47.019 --> 00:14:48.254
I think the Google lawsuit,

00:14:48.254 --> 00:14:51.423 align:start size:81% position:19%
a judge did not
rule in our favor.

00:14:53.092 --> 00:14:55.094
So that's something
that legislatively

00:14:55.094 --> 00:14:58.898
I've continued to push
through either abolishing

00:14:58.898 --> 00:15:00.633
or reforming section 230,

00:15:00.633 --> 00:15:03.836
so that big tech monopolies
like Google and Facebook,

00:15:03.836 --> 00:15:07.339
do not have this legal
immunity that allows them

00:15:07.339 --> 00:15:09.808
to do whatever they
want essentially

00:15:09.808 --> 00:15:13.112
and defying the whole purpose of

00:15:13.112 --> 00:15:16.882
what section 230
was created for.

00:15:16.882 --> 00:15:19.018
Which was to say, hey,
you know, let's have fair

00:15:19.018 --> 00:15:22.554
and neutral platforms online
for people to kind of have

00:15:22.554 --> 00:15:24.256
this public square.

00:15:24.256 --> 00:15:27.059
Google and Facebook and
others have taken that

00:15:27.059 --> 00:15:30.663
and abused it and have turned
themselves into publishers

00:15:30.663 --> 00:15:34.533 align:start size:97% position:3%
by picking and choosing what
information those online

00:15:34.533 --> 00:15:37.836
actually get to see
and sequestering or
censoring others,

00:15:37.836 --> 00:15:39.104
you know all about this.

00:15:41.607 --> 00:15:43.375
But they're not held
to the same standard

00:15:43.375 --> 00:15:45.611
that the New York
Times is held to,

00:15:45.611 --> 00:15:47.913
where New York Times picks
and chooses what stories,

00:15:47.913 --> 00:15:49.882 align:start size:94% position:6%
what letters to the editor
what op-eds they choose

00:15:49.882 --> 00:15:51.750
because they are publishers.

00:15:51.750 --> 00:15:55.187
These big tech monopolies
are acting as publishers

00:15:55.187 --> 00:15:58.257
but they're not held to
the same legal standard

00:15:58.257 --> 00:16:00.859 align:start size:84% position:16%
that any other
publisher is held to.

00:16:00.859 --> 00:16:02.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
And those were the
reforms that I was pushing

00:16:02.761 --> 00:16:03.929
through my legislation.

00:16:03.929 --> 00:16:05.331 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Do you sense
though that the ship

00:16:05.331 --> 00:16:06.799
has probably just
sailed on that?

00:16:06.799 --> 00:16:08.801 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, Trump was sort
of trying to do it

00:16:08.801 --> 00:16:11.337
and the Republicans were
always threatening about it

00:16:11.337 --> 00:16:12.972 align:start size:84% position:16%
but they don't,
and having hearings

00:16:12.972 --> 00:16:14.440 align:start size:84% position:16%
but they just
never did anything.

00:16:14.440 --> 00:16:17.042 align:start size:97% position:3%
Do you sense that there's
just no reason at this point?

00:16:17.042 --> 00:16:18.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
- I don't think we should
give, I don't think

00:16:18.944 --> 00:16:20.179
we can give up this fight.

00:16:20.179 --> 00:16:21.880
Because there's so
much at stake here.

00:16:21.880 --> 00:16:23.882
Social media has become

00:16:23.882 --> 00:16:26.485 align:start size:84% position:16%
such a part of so
many people's lives.

00:16:26.485 --> 00:16:28.854
And as we are seeing here today,

00:16:28.854 --> 00:16:31.957
what is happening at
the Capitol where,

00:16:33.125 --> 00:16:34.393
I know the updates
are still coming in,

00:16:34.393 --> 00:16:35.594
but before we started,

00:16:35.594 --> 00:16:37.329 align:start size:84% position:16%
I saw there was at
least one person shot,

00:16:37.329 --> 00:16:39.665 align:start size:88% position:13%
multiple Capitol police
have been injured.

00:16:41.467 --> 00:16:46.338 align:start size:97% position:3%
The algorithms that the social
media companies are using

00:16:46.338 --> 00:16:51.076
to intentionally manipulate
and control the information

00:16:51.076 --> 00:16:53.512
that their users are getting,

00:16:53.512 --> 00:16:58.517
has a direct role to play
in inciting this kind of

00:17:00.119 --> 00:17:02.454 align:start size:97% position:3%
frankly anarchy and
violence that we're seeing.

00:17:02.454 --> 00:17:05.958
And so we can't just say,
well, man, it's too late.

00:17:05.958 --> 00:17:08.427
We can't hold them accountable.

00:17:08.427 --> 00:17:10.529 align:start size:97% position:3%
I think we have to continue
to push our leaders.

00:17:10.529 --> 00:17:12.564 align:start size:84% position:16%
Those who on the
one hand are saying,

00:17:12.564 --> 00:17:15.267 align:start size:88% position:13%
hey, we're against
censorship by big tech,

00:17:15.267 --> 00:17:18.003
but on the other hand are not
backing that up with action

00:17:18.003 --> 00:17:21.707 align:start position:0%
and actually passing legislation
to do something about it.

00:17:21.707 --> 00:17:23.275 align:start size:84% position:16%
I think it's because
a lot of them

00:17:23.275 --> 00:17:25.277
are getting a lot
of fricking' money,

00:17:25.277 --> 00:17:27.046 align:start size:81% position:19%
from the Facebooks
and the Googles

00:17:27.046 --> 00:17:28.580 align:start size:84% position:16%
that their fundraisers
that they're doing

00:17:28.580 --> 00:17:30.249 align:start size:97% position:3%
at night and saying, oh
yeah, you know, don't worry

00:17:30.249 --> 00:17:31.683
I'll just talk about it

00:17:31.683 --> 00:17:32.684 align:start size:97% position:3%
but we're not actually
gonna do anything about it.

00:17:32.684 --> 00:17:33.919
- Yeah, so to that point,

00:17:33.919 --> 00:17:35.854 align:start size:84% position:16%
when you were doing
congressional hearings

00:17:35.854 --> 00:17:39.091 align:start size:97% position:3%
on quite literally anything,
did you often feel,

00:17:39.091 --> 00:17:41.393
'cause I think a lot of
people now feel this way

00:17:41.393 --> 00:17:43.328 align:start size:84% position:16%
that the whole thing
is just theater?

00:17:43.328 --> 00:17:44.563
That it's not really--

00:17:44.563 --> 00:17:46.165
- So much of it is.

00:17:46.165 --> 00:17:47.399
- 'Cause believe
me I watched enough

00:17:47.399 --> 00:17:49.034
of the social media
stuff especially,

00:17:49.034 --> 00:17:50.569
and it's like there
are guys up there

00:17:50.569 --> 00:17:53.205 align:start size:97% position:3%
saying things that I agree
with on the social media front

00:17:53.205 --> 00:17:55.407 align:start size:84% position:16%
especially Ted Cruz
kept hitting the stuff

00:17:55.407 --> 00:17:56.809
that I really think is right.

00:17:56.809 --> 00:17:59.945
And yet I'm going, but
nobody's doing anything.

00:17:59.945 --> 00:18:03.015
So you're saying, okay, Jack
from Twitter broke the law

00:18:03.015 --> 00:18:05.617 align:start size:94% position:6%
because he lied under
oath about shadow banning

00:18:05.617 --> 00:18:07.553 align:start size:88% position:13%
or whatever the
specific thing might be.

00:18:07.553 --> 00:18:08.787
But it's like, no
one does anything.

00:18:08.787 --> 00:18:10.722
So it's just like this
dog and pony show like,

00:18:10.722 --> 00:18:12.324 align:start size:88% position:13%
oh we're all pretending
to go to work

00:18:12.324 --> 00:18:15.260 align:start size:97% position:3%
and then we have drinks
together and then that's it.

00:18:15.260 --> 00:18:18.464 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Yeah, so much of it is
absolutely political theater

00:18:18.464 --> 00:18:20.032
and just for show.

00:18:20.032 --> 00:18:24.503 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I think that
there's an opportunity

00:18:24.503 --> 00:18:27.039 align:start size:84% position:16%
to hold more leaders
accountable given

00:18:27.039 --> 00:18:30.375
how much more access to,

00:18:31.543 --> 00:18:33.212 align:start size:88% position:13%
I think this is where
social media can be used

00:18:33.212 --> 00:18:35.914
in a positive way,
is to be able to

00:18:37.349 --> 00:18:40.986
not allow this kind of stuff
to go unchecked and say, hey,

00:18:40.986 --> 00:18:43.388 align:start size:97% position:3%
we're tracking, so, okay,
you're complaining about this,

00:18:43.388 --> 00:18:44.656
where's the bill?

00:18:44.656 --> 00:18:46.825 align:start size:81% position:19%
Have you talked
to your colleagues

00:18:46.825 --> 00:18:48.760 align:start size:84% position:16%
about trying to pass
this legislation?

00:18:48.760 --> 00:18:51.697
Are you building support for
it rather than just saying,

00:18:51.697 --> 00:18:53.866
okay, well, I'm gonna
put out a statement

00:18:53.866 --> 00:18:57.836
and then fundraise off that
statement but not actually

00:18:57.836 --> 00:19:00.906 align:start size:97% position:3%
do anything about, and
again this elections thing,

00:19:00.906 --> 00:19:03.976
I keep going back to
it because you know,

00:19:03.976 --> 00:19:06.245
we're living through it now.

00:19:06.245 --> 00:19:08.046
And if all the people
who were complaining

00:19:08.046 --> 00:19:11.250 align:start position:0%
about it now had actually
stepped up as leaders and said,

00:19:11.250 --> 00:19:13.485
okay, we have a big
election coming up.

00:19:13.485 --> 00:19:17.156 align:start size:97% position:3%
Let's fix these problems
before the election happens.

00:19:17.156 --> 00:19:21.360 align:start size:97% position:3%
There's bipartisan agreement
that this is a big issue.

00:19:21.360 --> 00:19:24.329 align:start size:97% position:3%
It should have been fixed
before this massive election

00:19:24.329 --> 00:19:25.998
in 2020 that we all
knew was coming.

00:19:25.998 --> 00:19:27.599
- It's so interesting,
'cause I said on the show

00:19:27.599 --> 00:19:30.769
this morning, it's like I'm
completely against violence,

00:19:30.769 --> 00:19:33.138
political violence
either way, for sure,

00:19:33.138 --> 00:19:35.240
full stop, like no doubt.

00:19:35.240 --> 00:19:38.911
And yet the people that are
doing some of this stuff,

00:19:38.911 --> 00:19:41.513 align:start size:88% position:13%
who've been called Nazis
and racists who said,

00:19:41.513 --> 00:19:44.049
okay, you know, who
see videos online

00:19:44.049 --> 00:19:46.518 align:start position:0%
of what may be election
tampering and all of this stuff.

00:19:46.518 --> 00:19:48.754
And they're told, they're not
supposed to see what they see

00:19:48.754 --> 00:19:51.690 align:start size:97% position:3%
or they don't see it or
they're conspiracy theorists.

00:19:51.690 --> 00:19:53.425 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then we'll get to
more of this in a moment.

00:19:53.425 --> 00:19:55.627
But like then we lock
people in their houses

00:19:55.627 --> 00:19:57.496
and we don't let
them to go to work.

00:19:57.496 --> 00:19:59.398
It's like, that's what I
mean when I said earlier

00:19:59.398 --> 00:20:02.434 align:start size:97% position:3%
like it sort of all felt
like it was gonna end up here

00:20:02.434 --> 00:20:05.671
in a weird sense that we've
just ramped up the crazy

00:20:05.671 --> 00:20:07.639
in so many ways that,

00:20:07.639 --> 00:20:10.609 align:start size:84% position:16%
well, people
storming the Capitol,

00:20:11.777 --> 00:20:13.412
again, not condoning
it, but it's like,

00:20:13.412 --> 00:20:15.247
of course it was gonna happen.

00:20:15.247 --> 00:20:18.517 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Well' we have to
understand how we got here

00:20:18.517 --> 00:20:20.686
and why we got here.

00:20:20.686 --> 00:20:23.622
One of the things that
has so frustrated me

00:20:23.622 --> 00:20:26.959
in our politics that I've
seen throughout my time

00:20:26.959 --> 00:20:31.463 line:0%
in Congress is how reactive
our so-called leaders are.

00:20:31.463 --> 00:20:35.267 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
They're not actually
leaders who are exercising

00:20:35.267 --> 00:20:39.638 line:0%
good judgment and foresight
to see, okay, if we do this,

00:20:39.638 --> 00:20:43.742
then it's likely to end up
with a certain consequence.

00:20:46.011 --> 00:20:47.846
And in situations like this,

00:20:47.846 --> 00:20:51.483 align:start size:84% position:16%
I think we'll see a
lot of reactions start
to come out of it

00:20:51.483 --> 00:20:54.386 align:start size:97% position:3%
but probably not a whole
lot of introspection to say,

00:20:54.386 --> 00:20:58.857
hey, how did we get here
so that we can make sure

00:20:58.857 --> 00:21:01.593
that we shift course
that we correct course

00:21:01.593 --> 00:21:04.630 align:start size:94% position:6%
and try to get back on
track to prevent this kind

00:21:04.630 --> 00:21:08.033 align:start size:97% position:3%
of situation from worsening
or happening again.

00:21:08.033 --> 00:21:10.869
That's really where the
leadership comes in,

00:21:10.869 --> 00:21:13.438 align:start size:84% position:16%
that we the American
people need,

00:21:13.438 --> 00:21:14.673
we've needed all along

00:21:14.673 --> 00:21:16.541 align:start size:84% position:16%
and we especially
need at this moment.

00:21:16.541 --> 00:21:19.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Yeah, so I wanna go into
a couple of the things

00:21:19.177 --> 00:21:21.079
'cause you kind of went
out in a blaze of glory,

00:21:21.079 --> 00:21:23.982 align:start size:97% position:3%
just like saying everything
that you believe.

00:21:23.982 --> 00:21:27.386
At least a whole bunch
of it at the very least

00:21:27.386 --> 00:21:30.722 align:start size:97% position:3%
and putting these bills
forward and everything else.

00:21:30.722 --> 00:21:32.357
But before we get into
the specifics of that,

00:21:32.357 --> 00:21:37.229 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm curious, do you sense
that someone like you

00:21:37.229 --> 00:21:39.931
has a future in the
democratic party?

00:21:39.931 --> 00:21:42.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
I get your frustrations
with Democrat, Republican,

00:21:42.401 --> 00:21:44.069
left, right and all
that kind of thing.

00:21:44.069 --> 00:21:48.373
But do you sense that sort
of the more moderate antiwar,

00:21:48.373 --> 00:21:52.210 align:start position:0%
don't want government doing
absolutely everything Democrat,

00:21:52.210 --> 00:21:54.012
does that exist anymore?

00:21:56.481 --> 00:22:01.386
- It's becoming more and
more rare in Washington.

00:22:02.821 --> 00:22:06.825
I think if, and I don't think
this is a recent phenomena,

00:22:08.460 --> 00:22:12.397 align:start size:84% position:16%
but if I look at the
interactions that
I've had with people

00:22:12.397 --> 00:22:14.666 align:start size:84% position:16%
throughout my campaign
for president,

00:22:15.834 --> 00:22:19.504 align:start size:84% position:16%
the conversations
and the social media

00:22:19.504 --> 00:22:22.507 align:start size:97% position:3%
and discussions that are
occurring across the country

00:22:22.507 --> 00:22:24.276
with people scratching
their heads at kind of

00:22:24.276 --> 00:22:27.012
the crazy things that
Congress is choosing

00:22:27.012 --> 00:22:29.681
to prioritize and
take action on.

00:22:29.681 --> 00:22:34.353
I think that there are
a majority of people,

00:22:34.353 --> 00:22:37.322
maybe most people who are hungry

00:22:37.322 --> 00:22:40.525 align:start size:84% position:16%
for some leadership
based on common sense,

00:22:40.525 --> 00:22:44.830
and leadership that values
our fundamental freedoms,

00:22:44.830 --> 00:22:48.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
as Americans in the
United States of America.

00:22:50.068 --> 00:22:52.170 align:start size:84% position:16%
We're not all going
to agree on everything

00:22:52.170 --> 00:22:54.139
or maybe even many things,

00:22:54.139 --> 00:22:58.477
but I know that we are
better when we are able

00:22:58.477 --> 00:23:02.180 align:start size:97% position:3%
to come together and have
honest and real discussions.

00:23:02.180 --> 00:23:04.483 align:start size:88% position:13%
Even bringing our
differences to the table

00:23:04.483 --> 00:23:07.786 align:start position:0%
when we are centered and focused
on what we can do together

00:23:07.786 --> 00:23:09.354 align:start size:81% position:19%
for the betterment
of our country.

00:23:09.354 --> 00:23:11.990
- So do you sense though,
that can happen with kind

00:23:11.990 --> 00:23:13.492
of the new wing
of the Democrats?

00:23:13.492 --> 00:23:15.527 align:start size:97% position:3%
Like, I don't know if you
were ever in like a sit-down

00:23:15.527 --> 00:23:19.364 align:start size:97% position:3%
with AOC and Ilhan and
Rashida and the rest of them.

00:23:19.364 --> 00:23:21.700
But do you sense if you came in,

00:23:21.700 --> 00:23:24.970
on what I would call your
extremely moderate position

00:23:24.970 --> 00:23:27.005
on abortion, that
almost everyone

00:23:27.005 --> 00:23:29.341
on the left would
have agreed with,

00:23:29.341 --> 00:23:32.511
literally five years ago,
certainly 10 years ago,

00:23:32.511 --> 00:23:35.280 align:start size:94% position:6%
where now you'd be
called an evil Republican

00:23:35.280 --> 00:23:39.050 align:start position:0%
or an evil conservative or
worse for having that position.

00:23:39.050 --> 00:23:40.385
Do you sense that
they're willing

00:23:40.385 --> 00:23:41.853
to have those conversations?

00:23:41.853 --> 00:23:43.422 align:start position:0%
I don't think it's the moderates
that are having the problem

00:23:43.422 --> 00:23:44.523
with the conversation.

00:23:45.924 --> 00:23:47.058
- I don't.

00:23:48.460 --> 00:23:50.429 align:start size:81% position:19%
I don't think that
there is really

00:23:50.429 --> 00:23:52.631
even an interest there, sadly.

00:23:54.332 --> 00:23:58.904 align:start size:97% position:3%
I think that it's indicative
of a group of people

00:24:00.038 --> 00:24:04.576 align:start size:84% position:16%
who are, you're
either all or nothing.

00:24:04.576 --> 00:24:07.679
You are either pure
enough in their eyes,

00:24:07.679 --> 00:24:09.781 align:start size:84% position:16%
whatever that means
and whatever barometer

00:24:09.781 --> 00:24:12.317 align:start size:97% position:3%
with which they're choosing
to measure a person by,

00:24:13.485 --> 00:24:15.921
or you're canceled.

00:24:15.921 --> 00:24:16.755
I think that's,

00:24:18.223 --> 00:24:19.891
and it's a dangerous place

00:24:19.891 --> 00:24:21.793
and something that
doesn't represent

00:24:23.195 --> 00:24:25.330
the freedom of thought
and the freedom of speech

00:24:25.330 --> 00:24:28.333 align:start size:88% position:13%
that we should celebrate
in this country.

00:24:28.333 --> 00:24:29.568
- So with that in mind,

00:24:29.568 --> 00:24:31.069
I saw an awful lot
of people on Twitter

00:24:31.069 --> 00:24:32.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
and although I do say
Twitter is not real life.

00:24:32.771 --> 00:24:35.073
I saw a lot of people when
you were campaigning saying,

00:24:35.073 --> 00:24:38.577
"man if Tulsi would just
say, she's a Republican,

00:24:39.711 --> 00:24:41.179
"she'd have a lot more support."

00:24:41.179 --> 00:24:43.215 align:start size:88% position:13%
That in essence you
would be sort of a more

00:24:43.215 --> 00:24:46.651
libertarian minded
centrist, Republican,

00:24:46.651 --> 00:24:48.153
something like that.

00:24:48.153 --> 00:24:50.622 align:start size:97% position:3%
And again, I get it, the two
party thing and all that.

00:24:50.622 --> 00:24:52.824 align:start size:88% position:13%
But if you were to have
a political future,

00:24:52.824 --> 00:24:54.626 align:start size:81% position:19%
would that make
some sense to you?

00:24:56.027 --> 00:24:58.230
- It's not something I've
I've given thought to.

00:24:58.230 --> 00:24:59.698
And I don't know.

00:24:59.698 --> 00:25:02.334
I think again, I point
to some deeper challenges

00:25:05.570 --> 00:25:08.206
that we need to address as
a people and as a country,

00:25:08.206 --> 00:25:12.978
and that we need to
look to our leaders

00:25:12.978 --> 00:25:16.715
to bring about this deeper
kind of spiritual change,

00:25:16.715 --> 00:25:18.650
that's gotta come
from the heart.

00:25:18.650 --> 00:25:21.419
Where there's a shift
towards working for

00:25:21.419 --> 00:25:23.388
and serving the people,

00:25:23.388 --> 00:25:28.393 align:start position:0%
rather than purely being
motivated by political ambition,

00:25:30.028 --> 00:25:33.698
greed, power and all
the selfishness that
frankly is driving

00:25:33.698 --> 00:25:35.400
so much of our politics today.

00:25:35.400 --> 00:25:36.635
- Yeah can you talk
a little bit more

00:25:36.635 --> 00:25:38.703
about how your faith
plays a role in this?

00:25:38.703 --> 00:25:41.740
'Cause it's pretty
rare to hear anyone

00:25:41.740 --> 00:25:44.876 align:start size:97% position:3%
that's thought of as somewhat
left to talk about faith.

00:25:44.876 --> 00:25:47.112 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I know even
during Christmas week

00:25:47.112 --> 00:25:48.914
and a few times over the
last couple of months,

00:25:48.914 --> 00:25:50.949
you've tweeted out a few things,

00:25:50.949 --> 00:25:52.717 align:start size:84% position:16%
a little bit talking
about your faith.

00:25:52.717 --> 00:25:56.254
And I do sense we're in
some sort of very odd,

00:25:56.254 --> 00:25:59.024
spiritual war right now.

00:25:59.024 --> 00:26:00.525
It's not like my
favorite language,

00:26:00.525 --> 00:26:02.928
but we are in some thing
where everyone's obsessed

00:26:02.928 --> 00:26:05.597
with politics but that's
really just a replacement

00:26:05.597 --> 00:26:06.565
for something else.

00:26:08.500 --> 00:26:09.534
- You know, this is,

00:26:10.735 --> 00:26:15.006
for me personally, my
relationship with God

00:26:15.006 --> 00:26:20.011
and my striving daily to
develop my love for God

00:26:21.212 --> 00:26:24.382
and to be pleasing
to God, by serving

00:26:24.382 --> 00:26:27.285 align:start size:84% position:16%
and taking care of
God's children and
protecting our planet,

00:26:27.285 --> 00:26:30.255 align:start size:84% position:16%
this is what motivates
me in my life.

00:26:30.255 --> 00:26:33.858
And regardless of the name

00:26:33.858 --> 00:26:37.629
with which people
choose to call God

00:26:37.629 --> 00:26:40.131
or how one worship
God or whatever,

00:26:40.131 --> 00:26:41.566
this is not about religion

00:26:41.566 --> 00:26:45.070 align:start size:97% position:3%
or one religion versus another
one, set versus another.

00:26:45.070 --> 00:26:50.075 align:start position:0%
This is to me about the
recognition in a very deep way,

00:26:51.509 --> 00:26:55.580
of who we are and seeing past
all of the different labels

00:26:58.116 --> 00:27:00.852
that are so often
used to divide us.

00:27:00.852 --> 00:27:03.221
And if we see each
other for who we are

00:27:03.221 --> 00:27:04.856
that we are all children of God,

00:27:04.856 --> 00:27:07.459
regardless of all
of the things that,

00:27:07.459 --> 00:27:10.328 align:start size:97% position:3%
again, those labels, those
things that are used to put us

00:27:10.328 --> 00:27:12.063
in different boxes,

00:27:12.063 --> 00:27:15.333
then we can come from
a place as individuals,

00:27:15.333 --> 00:27:17.068 align:start size:88% position:13%
and especially as
leaders in this country

00:27:17.068 --> 00:27:22.073 align:start position:0%
who carry a great
responsibility to make an impact

00:27:23.208 --> 00:27:24.809
on people's lives,
positive or negative.

00:27:24.809 --> 00:27:27.512
When we come from this
very deep spiritual place

00:27:27.512 --> 00:27:32.517
of a recognition of who we
are, then we're motivated

00:27:33.785 --> 00:27:36.621
by the most perfect motivation,

00:27:36.621 --> 00:27:39.991
which is really truly
to care for each other

00:27:39.991 --> 00:27:43.662 align:start size:97% position:3%
and to help each other to
help make that positive impact

00:27:43.662 --> 00:27:44.896
from wherever we sit,

00:27:44.896 --> 00:27:46.965
whether you're sitting
in the halls of Congress

00:27:46.965 --> 00:27:51.536
or sitting as we are in a
conversation here today.

00:27:51.536 --> 00:27:53.304
- Good God, I can't
believe they went

00:27:53.304 --> 00:27:54.839
with Kamala instead of you.

00:27:54.839 --> 00:27:56.074
It's making me...

00:27:58.143 --> 00:28:00.211
With that in mind I
think you you tried

00:28:00.211 --> 00:28:03.148 align:start size:84% position:16%
to add a little
honesty and decency

00:28:03.148 --> 00:28:04.916
and everything that
you just described

00:28:04.916 --> 00:28:06.584
in your last few
weeks in Congress.

00:28:06.584 --> 00:28:08.653 align:start size:88% position:13%
So I want to go through
a few of the things

00:28:08.653 --> 00:28:10.555 align:start size:84% position:16%
that you were
really talking about

00:28:10.555 --> 00:28:12.157
and trying to make happen.

00:28:12.157 --> 00:28:13.858
Let's talk about
the COVID vaccine.

00:28:13.858 --> 00:28:15.260
'Cause you've been
pretty outspoken

00:28:15.260 --> 00:28:17.162
about how we've really butchered

00:28:17.162 --> 00:28:19.264
some of what we're doing here,

00:28:19.264 --> 00:28:20.465
in terms of the rollout.

00:28:21.766 --> 00:28:24.869
- This may shock people
but I really strongly

00:28:24.869 --> 00:28:28.673
have been pushing our CDC and
their advisory committees,

00:28:28.673 --> 00:28:31.242 align:start size:94% position:6%
as well as our state
leadership here in Hawaii,

00:28:31.242 --> 00:28:33.778 align:start size:94% position:6%
leaders across the country
to make their decisions

00:28:33.778 --> 00:28:35.747
based on medical science.

00:28:35.747 --> 00:28:38.817 align:start size:84% position:16%
About who should
receive this vaccine,

00:28:38.817 --> 00:28:41.453 align:start size:88% position:13%
what's the priority,
given the limited amount

00:28:41.453 --> 00:28:44.289
of vaccine available, who
needs to receive it first?

00:28:44.289 --> 00:28:47.058
If you look at medical
science, you would find

00:28:47.058 --> 00:28:50.995
that based on the, all of the
trials that have been done

00:28:50.995 --> 00:28:52.964 align:start size:94% position:6%
it has been
scientifically established

00:28:52.964 --> 00:28:55.500
that this vaccine is effective

00:28:55.500 --> 00:28:57.902
in preventing serious
health complications

00:28:57.902 --> 00:29:00.505
from COVID and even death.

00:29:00.505 --> 00:29:02.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
It has not been
scientifically established

00:29:02.941 --> 00:29:07.946 align:start size:97% position:3%
that this vaccine is effective
in stopping this virus

00:29:09.314 --> 00:29:11.382 align:start size:97% position:3%
from being transmitted
from one person to another.

00:29:11.382 --> 00:29:15.086
So if you look at
both of those facts

00:29:15.086 --> 00:29:17.489 align:start size:97% position:3%
that have been
scientifically established,

00:29:17.489 --> 00:29:21.192 align:start size:97% position:3%
you would draw the conclusion
that the first priority

00:29:21.192 --> 00:29:23.661 align:start size:84% position:16%
of people who should
get this vaccine

00:29:23.661 --> 00:29:27.065
are our frontline healthcare
workers and elderly Americans.

00:29:27.065 --> 00:29:30.235
Those who are over
65 years of age,

00:29:30.235 --> 00:29:35.006 align:start position:0%
and who have been proven
throughout this entire pandemic

00:29:35.006 --> 00:29:38.777
are many, many times
more likely to die,

00:29:38.777 --> 00:29:40.512
if they get this virus

00:29:40.512 --> 00:29:43.081
than those who are
younger and healthy.

00:29:45.049 --> 00:29:48.219
Unfortunately the
recommendations
that are coming out

00:29:48.219 --> 00:29:50.522
of the CDC do not reflect

00:29:50.522 --> 00:29:52.624 align:start size:88% position:13%
what has been
established by science.

00:29:52.624 --> 00:29:55.326
And this is the warning
that I'm calling out.

00:29:55.326 --> 00:29:56.861
So what is that?

00:29:56.861 --> 00:29:57.862
What is going on in the CDC?
- What they're recommending

00:29:57.862 --> 00:30:00.498
essentially is they have,

00:30:02.200 --> 00:30:04.269 align:start size:94% position:6%
they're making politically
driven decisions

00:30:04.269 --> 00:30:06.104 align:start size:84% position:16%
that are essentially
putting the lives

00:30:06.104 --> 00:30:08.673
of elderly American
seniors at risk.

00:30:08.673 --> 00:30:10.074
Where they're saying,

00:30:10.074 --> 00:30:11.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
okay, well, yes frontline
healthcare workers

00:30:11.543 --> 00:30:13.945
are getting it first as
they should right now.

00:30:13.945 --> 00:30:17.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
But those who are getting
it next are people

00:30:17.415 --> 00:30:19.918
who they deem as
essential workers.

00:30:19.918 --> 00:30:22.253
Which is about 87
million Americans.

00:30:22.253 --> 00:30:26.191
And those who fall
under everything from

00:30:27.392 --> 00:30:28.760
people who are working
at the grocery store,

00:30:28.760 --> 00:30:29.694 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
people who are manning
the cash register

00:30:29.694 --> 00:30:30.962 line:0%
at a liquor store, to lawyers,

00:30:30.962 --> 00:30:35.433 line:0%
to people working in the
media, to people working

00:30:36.768 --> 00:30:38.703 align:start size:97% position:3%
in transportation,
constructions, corrections.

00:30:38.703 --> 00:30:41.940
There's essentially a
laundry list of people

00:30:41.940 --> 00:30:46.811 align:start size:97% position:3%
who they have deemed as
essential workers of any age,

00:30:46.811 --> 00:30:49.881
who they're saying should
either get the vaccine

00:30:49.881 --> 00:30:51.182
before our seniors,

00:30:51.182 --> 00:30:53.918
or who are seniors
need to compete with,

00:30:53.918 --> 00:30:55.453
in order to get this vaccine.

00:30:55.453 --> 00:30:56.788
And this is what is,

00:30:59.290 --> 00:31:02.760 align:start position:0%
it's just mind boggling because
this is coming from people

00:31:02.760 --> 00:31:05.029
who claim to be medical experts,

00:31:05.029 --> 00:31:07.899
but they're not making their
decisions based on science.

00:31:07.899 --> 00:31:11.836 align:start position:0%
They're instead making
politically motivated decisions.

00:31:11.836 --> 00:31:14.706 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Where do you fall
generally on lockdowns

00:31:14.706 --> 00:31:15.940
and the rest of it?

00:31:15.940 --> 00:31:18.209
I mean, you know, we're
coming up unbelievably

00:31:18.209 --> 00:31:20.078
on basically almost a year.

00:31:20.078 --> 00:31:22.213 align:start size:88% position:13%
I mean, it's been
about 10 months already

00:31:22.213 --> 00:31:25.817
of sort of lockdowns,
masks, the whole thing.

00:31:25.817 --> 00:31:28.486
We were told two weeks
to flatten the curve.

00:31:28.486 --> 00:31:32.223
And now we're being told,
oh, maybe a hundred-day,

00:31:32.223 --> 00:31:34.726
federal mask mandate.

00:31:34.726 --> 00:31:37.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm in California where
everything is locked down.

00:31:37.495 --> 00:31:39.998 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, the main
street I live off of,

00:31:39.998 --> 00:31:41.199
it looks like a ghost town.

00:31:41.199 --> 00:31:43.268 align:start size:88% position:13%
I mean, it genuinely
looks like a ghost town.

00:31:44.702 --> 00:31:47.238
Do you believe this should
have been left to the States?

00:31:47.238 --> 00:31:50.108
And are you kind of shocked at
how it's now 10 months later

00:31:50.108 --> 00:31:52.644
and we kind of forget
where we started from?

00:31:55.313 --> 00:31:56.781
- I mean, there's no question

00:31:56.781 --> 00:31:59.651 align:start size:94% position:6%
that this is a major
public health issue given,

00:31:59.651 --> 00:32:01.486 align:start size:88% position:13%
not only how infectious
this virus is

00:32:01.486 --> 00:32:04.822 align:start size:97% position:3%
but also the recent mutation
that we've seen occur

00:32:04.822 --> 00:32:06.257
in the UK and other places.

00:32:06.257 --> 00:32:08.927
And now I think Colorado
has gotten the first few

00:32:08.927 --> 00:32:13.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
of an even more infectious
version of COVID.

00:32:13.564 --> 00:32:16.467 align:start size:88% position:13%
So I think that they're,
the baseline standard

00:32:16.467 --> 00:32:19.804 align:start size:97% position:3%
of public health precautions
do need to be taken,

00:32:19.804 --> 00:32:20.972
which you know it is.

00:32:22.106 --> 00:32:23.675 align:start size:88% position:13%
Wear a mask, protect
yourself, protect others

00:32:23.675 --> 00:32:26.444 align:start size:84% position:16%
and wash your hands
and socially distance.

00:32:27.779 --> 00:32:32.750 align:start position:0%
The lack of a national strategy
with regards to testing

00:32:34.118 --> 00:32:37.322 align:start position:0%
has worsened the situation
where still as we sit here today

00:32:37.322 --> 00:32:40.692 align:start size:88% position:13%
it is incredibly
difficult to get a test.

00:32:40.692 --> 00:32:44.329 align:start size:97% position:3%
If you test more
frequently and more people,

00:32:44.329 --> 00:32:46.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
then you have the
ability for people to act

00:32:46.164 --> 00:32:49.400 align:start size:97% position:3%
on that information and
take precautions themselves.

00:32:49.400 --> 00:32:51.669 align:start size:84% position:16%
There's no reason
why we shouldn't have
these capabilities

00:32:51.669 --> 00:32:53.938
deployed all across the country.

00:32:53.938 --> 00:32:56.774 align:start size:84% position:16%
There's no reason
why we shouldn't have
medical grade masks

00:32:56.774 --> 00:32:58.209
available to every American,

00:32:58.209 --> 00:33:01.913 align:start position:0%
which are actually most
effective versus the cloth masks

00:33:01.913 --> 00:33:03.281
that so many people
are forced to use

00:33:03.281 --> 00:33:05.583
because they can't
get medical masks.

00:33:05.583 --> 00:33:10.588
And then the issue with
the nonsensical decisions

00:33:11.789 --> 00:33:13.858
that a lot of state and
local leaders are making

00:33:13.858 --> 00:33:17.161
for example, in California,
I saw, I think it's a viral

00:33:17.161 --> 00:33:19.897 align:start size:97% position:3%
video at this point where this
guy is out paddle boarding

